# Bindings for the browser suite's `wrangler dev`, loaded via --env-file
# (see `playwright.config.ts`). Committed on purpose: every value is an
# obviously-fake local-only dummy, which is also why CI needs no secret.
#
# This is deliberately NOT `.dev.vars`. That file is read by the Vitest
# workers pool as well, and it overrides the bindings `vitest.config.ts` sets
# explicitly — putting SIGNIN_ALLOWLIST and BETTER_AUTH_URL there turned 56
# server tests red, because every signed-in test suddenly had a different
# allowlist and origin from the one it asserts against.
#
# It is also not `--var KEY:VALUE`, which mangles any value containing a
# colon: `--var BETTER_AUTH_URL:http://localhost:8787` produced an origin
# that matched nothing, so every POST failed the same-origin check with a
# bare 403 "Forbidden" that reads like an auth bug.

# wrangler.jsonc says "resend", which throws here with no RESEND_API_KEY —
# into an error signin.ts deliberately swallows, so it fails invisibly.
NOTIFIER=console

# Without this, magic links are minted against https://makethe.team and the
# same-origin check on every POST compares against production's origin.
BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:8787

BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=local-browser-tests-only-not-a-real-secret
CANCEL_TOKEN_SECRET=local-browser-tests-only-not-a-real-cancel-secret
RESPONSE_TOKEN_SECRET=local-browser-tests-only-not-a-real-secret

# Suppresses the send for anything else. The harness does not depend on this
# — see the header of `test/browser/sign-in.ts` for why.
SIGNIN_ALLOWLIST=owner@example.test,player@example.test,jamie@example.test

# `wrangler.jsonc` says 50, which is production's cost control (TR-31) and
# wrong for a test run. Measured 15 August 2026: a single clean pass of this
# suite sends 50 — it exhausts the ceiling exactly, and every test after that
# point runs with delivery refused as `daily-ceiling-reached`.
#
# That failed silently for sign-in, because `sign-in.ts` reads the magic-link
# token out of D1 rather than from an email, so the refusal changes nothing it
# depends on. It did not fail silently for the leave journey, which flaked once
# during the M7a merge for exactly this reason: a red test whose cause was the
# quota, not the code.
#
# Counted per UTC day in `email_quota`, which the pre-suite reset now clears —
# so this is about one run's own budget, not accumulation across runs. Finite
# rather than absent on purpose: a test that loops sending email should still
# hit a wall.
#
# The ceiling's real behaviour is covered where it can be asserted precisely,
# in the server suite, and must stay there.
MAX_EMAILS_PER_DAY=1000

# `wrangler.jsonc` says "webpush" now that push is live in production, and
# that branch calls `requireBinding` on VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY at notifier
# construction — which this suite has no access to, and deliberately should
# not: the header above is explicit that every value here is a fake and that
# CI therefore needs no secret. Left unpinned, every route that builds a
# notifier would 500 and the whole suite would fail on an infrastructure
# detail rather than on anything it is testing.
#
# Exactly the same reason NOTIFIER is pinned to "console" above.
#
# This also keeps `test/browser/push.spec.ts`'s dark-state assertions honest:
# with no VAPID key the account page renders the Notifications section and no
# button, which is a real state — every deployment before turn-on, and every
# local `wrangler dev` — not merely a test fiction.
PUSH_NOTIFIER=null

# `wrangler.jsonc` says "cloudflare" since M54, and that branch throws on every
# send because CLOUDFLARE_EMAIL_API_TOKEN is a secret this suite has no access
# to and deliberately should not have — the header above is explicit that every
# value here is a fake.
#
# It is not a quiet degradation. The throw propagates out of the welcome email
# and out of the cron that opens a fixture, so `seedWorld` ends with five
# fixtures still `scheduled` and every browser test fails in `beforeAll` — the
# suite and `guide:capture` with it. Found on 3 September 2026, while capturing
# the pages M55 changed.
#
# `vitest.config.ts` pins the same two for the same reason; browser.env was
# missed. `test/config/env-pinning.test.ts` is the guard that stops a
# third binding being pinned in one config and forgotten in the other.
EMAIL_SPILLOVER=none
EMAIL_WARMUP_PER_DAY=0
